  "schema": "fhf-harness/duplicate-selector-baseline/v1",
  "why": "ui-config-hierarchy rule 5 says a data-cy literal shared by two module configs belongs in common.ui.js, imported rather than redeclared. The rule was enforced with no baseline, so every config that already carried a duplicate was uneditable: measured 2026-09-05 at 103 duplicates across 22 of the ui config files. That is the same failure the dead-selector check next to it already avoids with a baseline, and an unusable gate gets switched off. Listed entries WARN; a duplicate that is not listed BLOCKS. One-directional: remove an entry when the literal moves to common.ui.js, never add one to silence a new duplicate. The lossMitigation/ and loss-mitigation/ keys for lossMitigationFilter.config.js are intentionally duplicated while the directory rename is in review - remove the lossMitigation/ key once front-end-automation has merged it.",
